          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. Two elements, A and B, have the following configurations —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.108,
            0.374,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A: 2, 8, 5 B: 2, 8, 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.129,
            0.49,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Which element is more reactive?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.146,
            0.772,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Will A and B form ionic or covalent bonds when they combine? Explain using electron transfer or sharing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.179,
            0.684,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Predict the formula of the compound they would form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.2,
            0.772,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14. Assertion (A): Copper sulfate conducts electricity in the molten state but not in the solid state."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.237,
            0.772,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reason (R): Copper and sulfate ions are fixed in the lattice in molten state, while in solid state they can move freely."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.275,
            0.39,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Choose the correct option:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.295,
            0.725,
            0.313
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.313,
            0.753,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.33,
            0.399,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) A is true, but R is false."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.346,
            0.399,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) A is false, but R is true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
